Activation: wait for a spawned service for as long as its process is alive.

MUST apply after unique-activation.patch (the "z" name sorts it last).

A fixed 25 s wait turned host load into a ServiceUnknown. xdg-desktop-portal
activates its backend before it claims org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop; the
portalshot probe's call (which includes that activation) takes 8.6 s on an
idle host and 18.8 s on a busy one, and on a busier one the 25 s ran out
while the frontend was still starting: "ServiceUnknown: The name
org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop was not provided by any .service files" after
~25 s, with the .service file present and the same 41 portal files as a
passing run (portalshottest.py x86_64: 2 of 10 runs failed on a host at load
average 46, 0 of 8 more on a quiet one). The message is the generic one
because send_msg turns every failed activation into reply_service_unknown.

A service that is running is slow, not failed. The wait now polls the spawned
child: while it lives the cap is ACTIVATION_ALIVE_CAP (120 s); once it has
exited without claiming the name only ACTIVATION_TIMEOUT (25 s) more is
given, so a service that really dies costs what it always did. A second
caller waiting on the same activation follows the spawner's in-flight marker.

--- a/src/peers.rs
+++ b/src/peers.rs
@@ -43,6 +43,15 @@
 /// timeout.
 const ACTIVATION_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(25);
 
+/// Upper bound on the wait for a spawned service that is still running. A
+/// service that is alive is slow, not failed: xdg-desktop-portal activates
+/// its backend before it claims its name and measured 8.6 s on an idle host,
+/// 18.8 s on a busy one and more than 25 s on a busier one, where every
+/// caller got ServiceUnknown for a service that came up moments later. A
+/// child that has exited without claiming the name still gets only
+/// `ACTIVATION_TIMEOUT` more.
+const ACTIVATION_ALIVE_CAP: Duration = Duration::from_secs(120);
+
 /// Poll interval while waiting for an activated service to claim its name.
 /// There's no notification hook into `NameRegistry` to await instead, so
 /// this is a plain poll loop; see `Peers::await_name_owner`.
